    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Regional Theatre is a 2026 studio album by British band The Fierce & The Dead, released through Spencer Park Music. Following News from the Invisible World, it develops the group’s adventurous blend of psychedelic rock, progressive music, post-rock, alternative metal, shoegaze, and experimental pop. The ten-track, roughly 37-minute set ranges from the driving “The 1234” and “Thrash” to the atmospheric “Dream Sequence” and “Signal Bleed,” balancing abrasive guitar textures with melodic, often unexpectedly spacious passages.\n\nThe album also marks a further evolution in the band’s lineup, with Kevin Feazey continuing as lead vocalist and Tom Hunt contributing keyboards, percussion, and backing vocals. Its lyrical focus on communication and the difficulty of genuine human interaction gives the music a contemporary thematic thread, while the band’s characteristic contrasts—grit against harmony, intensity against restraint—keep the arrangements unpredictable. Physical editions include a lyric booklet, while a limited vinyl package adds instrumental mixes, other rarities, and a specially written play script, emphasizing the album’s theatrical concept.",
